{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Not with our fathers.</b> Alone." "<b>But with us, us.</b> And the meaning is: also with us, like לא יקרא שמך עוד יעקב (your name shall no more be called Jacob). Or its meaning: He did not make a covenant with our fathers who were in Egypt, but with us He made the covenant, for there are many in the camp who heard the covenant from the mouth of HaShem. Therefore he said: us, those who are here and are alive. And the proof of the correctness of this interpretation is that he said, 'with you' and 'among you.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:23.798236817Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}